            "notes": "## Powers  \n\nIn most games, I take [Foresight](item_f4163ce1-8f80-43ca-85d4-39812084400f) because it makes it easier to land shots after blinking, giving you time to adjust your aim. It also scales with ammo (but **not** with [Quantum Clip](item_3a108115-ec6e-4b98-8074-1b015cf535f1), for some reason).  \n\nIf you don\u2019t like the aimbot power, you can take [Quantum Clip](item_3a108115-ec6e-4b98-8074-1b015cf535f1), which is a straightforward ammo upgrade. Pick powers from R5 and R7(including optional ones).\n\n## Items  \n\n[Stockpile](item_a113eb56-9999-4f22-9bd7-18f4dbd00cc2) and [Pulse Detector](item_79ddef46-8917-4d8f-a123-7ddb589ad3e7) are excellent picks since they both scale [Foresight](item_f4163ce1-8f80-43ca-85d4-39812084400f) and increase [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed). For poorer rounds, just keep [Ammo Reserves](item_982d53aa-5ef4-493f-93e7-9e374d0ebf34) over [Stockpile](item_a113eb56-9999-4f22-9bd7-18f4dbd00cc2).\n\n[Aftermarket Firing Pin](item_2485b212-b286-42d0-a2bd-20eb4396b054) is the least important item\u2014you can keep [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) and barely lose any damage.\n\nIf there are many armor targets, consider picking up [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27), since armor cuts your damage in about half.",
