            "notes": "## Powers \n\n[Quantum Clip](item_3a108115-ec6e-4b98-8074-1b015cf535f1) is 25% more ammo. Since it takes quite a bit of time to unload ammo now, attack speed is very good.\n\n## Items\n\nThis round you can buy either [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) or one of the other optional epic damage items you prefer. I usually get [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) because it just matches so well with Tracer. With it, you get 25% movement speed after blinking, another Weapon Jammer\u2013style boost (10% Attack Speed + Weapon Power), around 330 HP when active, and 10% Cooldown Reduction. Pulse Bomb is not a bad ult, but in Stadium it\u2019s much worse since enemies are often above 350 HP and there\u2019s usually a Kiriko with [Two-Zu](item_80f16d3e-a4c0-4fa8-90b1-a0f033a1a77b).\n\nIf you have enough money, consider upgrading [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) or [Pulse Detector](item_79ddef46-8917-4d8f-a123-7ddb589ad3e7) into [El-Sa'ka Suppressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100). At this stage in the game, the healing might be too hard to kill through without it.\n\nAlso consider swapping [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) for [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) if you see a lot of armor on the enemy team.",
